    <document-link format="text/html" url="https://ncics.org/news/events/u-s-india-climate-downscaling-workshop/">
      <title>
        <narrative>US-INDIA Partnership for Climate Resilence</narrative>
      </title>
      <description>
        <narrative>NOAA's Cooperative Institute for Climate and Satellites-North Carolina (CISESS-NC) is participated in and supported NOAA's  efforts to implement key elements of the U.S.-India Partnership for Climate Resilience (PCR) in collaboration with pertinent NCEI and other federal personnel particularly in support of technical cooperation. NA19NES4320002</narrative>
      </description>
      <category code="B11"/>
      <language code="en"/>
      <document-date iso-date="2019-05-01"/>
    </document-link>
    <document-link format="application/pdf" url="https://nmsmarineprotectedareas.blob.core.windows.net/marineprotectedareas-prod/media/archive/fac/products/mpa-fac-external-finance-report-jan-2017.pdf">
      <title>
        <narrative>Improving the capacity of Belize's Marine Protected Areas co-managers to address capacity needs identified by Gulf and Caribbean Fisheries Institute (GCFI) - MPA Connect network.  FY22</narrative>
      </title>
      <description>
        <narrative>Project that seeks to build capacity to address the management needs identified in the MPA Connect capacity needs assessment of 2017 for relevant Marine Protected Areas (MPA) sites in Belize. In realizing this objective, the project will include capacity-building for socioeconomic assessment and monitoring, strengthening of enforcement programs, and improving governance among marine protected areas co-managers. The socioeconomic assessment will also include an assessment of the implementation of Managed Access; a fisheries management program in Belize that requires an external evaluation engaging all stakeholders including fishers, fishing groups, NGOs, relevant private investors, and government departments and ministries. At least one knowledge product will be generated for sharing with the wider Caribbean MPA network to assist in building capacities regionally. NA22NOS4820176</narrative>
      </description>
      <category code="B02"/>
      <language code="en"/>
      <document-date iso-date="2017-01-02"/>
      <recipient-country code="BZ"/>
    </document-link>
    <document-link format="text/html" url="https://www.fws.gov/cites/cites-cop19">
      <title>
        <narrative>Conference of the Parties 2019</narrative>
      </title>
      <description>
        <narrative>Support the travel, subsistence, and accommodation of up to two delegates from developing countries to attend the meeting of the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora (CITES) Conference of the Parties. CITES regulates the conservation and sustainable use of biodiversity to ensure no species entering into international trade is threatened with extinction. There are currently 184 Parties to the Convention. Meetings occurred in Panama City, Panama in November 2022. The funding also contributes to the management and administration of the Sponsored Delegates Project. NA22NMF0150169</narrative>
      </description>
      <category code="B16"/>
      <language code="en"/>
      <document-date iso-date="2017-09-30"/>
      <recipient-country code="PA"/>
    </document-link>
